IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-dates`
IMPORT `spr-part8-credits-1`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06.
--
-- LAYER 1, PART 8 (3 of 3): regulations 34 to 39 (National Insurance credits, Chapter 3,
-- second part: child benefit, care of a child under 12, foster parents, carers, the
-- extra twelve weeks for carers, and the time limit for applications).
-- Written from the text alone and from no one's point of view.
-- Not among the inputs, so taken as plain inputs below: the qualifying earnings factor
-- and the earnings factors; the contents of the Fostering, Looked After Children and
-- Foster Placement Regulations and of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General)
-- Regulations 1987; whether the Secretary of State considers a level of care
-- appropriate; and the length of a "week" for the 12-week periods in regulation 38,
-- which is taken as seven days (fork F33).
-- Where an application is required, whether it was received "in accordance with
-- regulation 39" is a Boolean on the fact record; `regulation 39: the application is
-- received in time` (below) is the rule that decides it.

§ `Part 8: National Insurance Credits (continued)`

§§ `Chapter 3 (continued)`

§§§ `Regulation 34: credits in respect of an award of child benefit`

DECLARE ChildBenefitCreditFacts HAS
    `the person is awarded child benefit for any part of the week in respect of a child under the age of 12` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the partner of a person to whom child benefit is awarded for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person resides with the person to whom child benefit is awarded` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person shares responsibility with that person for the child in respect of whom child benefit is awarded` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person makes an application to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs to be so credited in accordance with regulation 39` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all the earnings factors of the person to whom child benefit is awarded for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `of those, the earnings factors derived from contributions credited by virtue of that person being awarded child benefit` IS A NUMBER
    `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER

-- src:423 | (4) In calculating the earnings factors for the purpose of paragraph (3), no account is to be taken of any earnings factors derived from contributions credited by virtue of that person being awarded child benefit.
@ref Regulation 34(4) (src:423)
GIVEN facts IS A ChildBenefitCreditFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 34(4): the earnings factors that count` facts MEANS
    facts's `all the earnings factors of the person to whom child benefit is awarded for the year` MINUS facts's `of those, the earnings factors derived from contributions credited by virtue of that person being awarded child benefit`

-- src:422 | (3) Paragraph (1)(b) only applies in respect of a week that falls within a year for which the earnings factors of the person to whom child benefit is awarded exceed the qualifying earnings factor.
@ref Regulation 34(3) (src:422)
GIVEN facts IS A ChildBenefitCreditFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 34(3): the week falls within a year for which the earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor` facts MEANS
    `regulation 34(4): the earnings factors that count` facts GREATER THAN facts's `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`

-- src:416 | (2) The circumstances are that the partner—
-- src:417 | (a) resides with the person to whom child benefit is awarded,
-- src:418 | (b) shares responsibility for the child in respect of whom child benefit is awarded with that person,
-- src:419 | (c) is ordinarily resident in Great Britain,
-- src:420 | (d) is not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody, and
-- src:421 | (e) makes an application to the Commissioners for Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs to be so credited in accordance with regulation 39.
@ref Regulation 34(2) (src:416-421)
GIVEN facts IS A ChildBenefitCreditFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 34(2): the circumstances are met` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person resides with the person to whom child benefit is awarded`
    AND facts's `the person shares responsibility with that person for the child in respect of whom child benefit is awarded`
    AND facts's `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain`
    AND NOT (facts's `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody`)
    AND facts's `the person makes an application to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs to be so credited in accordance with regulation 39`

-- src:413 | (1) A person is entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of a week in which the person is—
-- src:414 | (a) awarded child benefit for any part of that week in respect of a child under the age of 12, or
-- src:415 | (b) in the circumstances specified by paragraph (2) and subject to paragraph (3), the partner of a person to whom child benefit is awarded.
@ref Regulation 34(1) (src:413-415)
GIVEN facts IS A ChildBenefitCreditFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 34(1): the person is entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is awarded child benefit for any part of the week in respect of a child under the age of 12`
    OR (    facts's `the person is the partner of a person to whom child benefit is awarded for the week`
        AND `regulation 34(2): the circumstances are met` facts
        AND `regulation 34(3): the week falls within a year for which the earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor` facts)

§§§ `Regulation 35: credits for persons providing care for a child under the age of 12`

DECLARE CarerRelationship IS ONE OF
    `a non-resident parent of the child`
    `a grandparent of the child`
    `a great-grandparent of the child`
    `a great-great-grandparent of the child`
    `a sibling of the child`
    `a sibling of a parent of the child`
    `a spouse or former spouse of a person listed in regulation 35(6)(a) to (f)`
    `a civil partner or former civil partner of a person listed in regulation 35(6)(a) to (f)`
    `a partner or former partner of a person listed in regulation 35(6)(a) to (h)`
    `a son or daughter of a person listed in regulation 35(6)(e) to (i)`
    `in respect of a son or daughter of a person listed in regulation 35(6)(f), that person's spouse, former spouse, civil partner, former civil partner, partner or former partner`
    `none of the relationships listed in regulation 35(6)`

-- Gloss, paragraph (6): the relationship is one of the eleven the paragraph lists.
-- src:443 | (6) The person specified in paragraph (2)(b) is—
-- src:444 | (a) a non-resident parent;
-- src:445 | (b) a grandparent;
-- src:446 | (c) a great-grandparent;
-- src:447 | (d) a great-great-grandparent;
-- src:448 | (e) a sibling;
-- src:449 | (f) a parent’s sibling;
-- src:450 | (g) a spouse or former spouse of any persons listed in sub-paragraphs (a) to (f);
-- src:451 | (h) a civil partner or former civil partner of any persons listed in sub-paragraphs (a) to (f);
-- src:452 | (i) a partner or former partner of any persons listed in sub-paragraphs (a) to (h);
-- src:453 | (j) a son or daughter of any persons listed in sub-paragraphs (e) to (i);
-- src:454 | (k) in respect of a son or daughter of a person listed in sub-paragraph (f), that person’s—
-- src:455 | (i) spouse or former spouse,
-- src:456 | (ii) civil partner or former civil partner, or
-- src:457 | (iii) partner or former partner.
@ref Regulation 35(6) (src:443-457)
GIVEN relationship IS A CarerRelationship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 35(6): the relationship is one the paragraph specifies` relationship MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `none of the relationships listed in regulation 35(6)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Gloss, paragraph (8): a "partner" for paragraphs (6)(i) and (k)(iii) is the other member
-- of a couple who are not married or civil partners but live together as if they were.
-- src:459 | (8) For the purposes of paragraph (6)(i) and (k)(iii), a partner is a person who is the other member of a couple who are not married to, or civil partners of, each other but are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
@ref Regulation 35(8) (src:459)
GIVEN `the person is the other member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the couple are married to, or civil partners of, each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the couple are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 35(8): the person is a partner` `the person is the other member of a couple` `the couple are married to, or civil partners of, each other` `the couple are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners` MEANS
        `the person is the other member of a couple`
    AND NOT (`the couple are married to, or civil partners of, each other`)
    AND `the couple are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners`

-- Gloss, paragraph (7): "sibling" in (6)(e) and (f) includes a half-blood, step and adopted sibling.
-- src:458 | (7) For the purposes of paragraph (6)(e) and (f), a sibling includes a sibling of the half blood, a step sibling and an adopted sibling.
@ref Regulation 35(7) (src:458)
GIVEN `the person is a sibling of the whole blood` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a sibling of the half blood` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a step sibling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an adopted sibling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 35(7): the person counts as a sibling` `the person is a sibling of the whole blood` `the person is a sibling of the half blood` `the person is a step sibling` `the person is an adopted sibling` MEANS
        `the person is a sibling of the whole blood`
    OR `the person is a sibling of the half blood`
    OR `the person is a step sibling`
    OR `the person is an adopted sibling`

DECLARE CarerElection IS ONE OF
    `no other person can satisfy paragraph (3)(a)(i), so paragraph (4) does not arise`
    `the person is the carer credited`
    `another carer is the carer credited`
    `the Secretary of State has not yet decided which carer is credited`

-- Gloss, paragraph (4): when more than one person can satisfy (3)(a)(i) for a week, they
-- elect, with B's agreement, which of them is credited, and only that person is; failing
-- agreement the Secretary of State decides. The text does not say what the person is
-- entitled to while no election has been agreed and the Secretary of State has not yet
-- decided; the encoding says so in the last constructor (fork F35).
-- src:436 | (4) Where the requirements relating to the provision of care by A in paragraph (3)(a)(i) can be satisfied by more than one person in respect of a week in which B was awarded child benefit—
-- src:437 | (a) those persons shall elect, with the agreement of B, which of them is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution credit (and then only the elected person is to be so credited), or
-- src:438 | (b) the Secretary of State is to exercise his discretion to determine which of those persons is to be credited with that contribution, in default of the agreement referred to in sub-paragraph (a).
@ref Regulation 35(4) (src:436-438)
GIVEN `the number of persons who can satisfy paragraph (3)(a)(i) for the week, including the person` IS A NUMBER
      `the carers have elected, with the agreement of B, which of them is to be credited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the carers elected the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has decided, in default of agreement, that the person is the one credited` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A CarerElection
`regulation 35(4): which carer is credited` `the number of persons who can satisfy paragraph (3)(a)(i) for the week, including the person` `the carers have elected, with the agreement of B, which of them is to be credited` `the carers elected the person` `the Secretary of State has decided, in default of agreement, that the person is the one credited` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons who can satisfy paragraph (3)(a)(i) for the week, including the person` AT MOST 1
    THEN `no other person can satisfy paragraph (3)(a)(i), so paragraph (4) does not arise`
    ELSE IF `the carers have elected, with the agreement of B, which of them is to be credited`
         THEN (IF `the carers elected the person` THEN `the person is the carer credited` ELSE `another carer is the carer credited`)
         ELSE CONSIDER `the Secretary of State has decided, in default of agreement, that the person is the one credited`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN `the Secretary of State has not yet decided which carer is credited`
              WHEN JUST decided THEN (IF decided THEN `the person is the carer credited` ELSE `another carer is the carer credited`)

DECLARE ChildCareApplication HAS
    `the application includes the name and date of birth of the child, or each child, cared for` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs have asked for a declaration by B that the conditions in paragraph (2) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application includes that declaration by B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application specifies the relevant week or weeks in which the child, or each child, was cared for` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:439 | (5) An application under paragraph (3)(c) must—
-- src:440 | (a) include the name and date of birth of the child , or each child, cared for,
-- src:441 | (b) where requested by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs, include a declaration by B that the conditions in paragraph (2) are satisfied, and
-- src:442 | (c) specify the relevant week or weeks in which the child , or each child, was cared for.
@ref Regulation 35(5) (src:439-442)
GIVEN application IS A ChildCareApplication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 35(5): the application has the required content` application MEANS
        application's `the application includes the name and date of birth of the child, or each child, cared for`
    AND (IF application's `the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs have asked for a declaration by B that the conditions in paragraph (2) are satisfied`
         THEN application's `the application includes that declaration by B`
         ELSE TRUE)
    AND application's `the application specifies the relevant week or weeks in which the child, or each child, was cared for`

DECLARE ChildCareFacts HAS
    `the person provided care in the week in respect of a child under the age of 12` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's relationship to the child` IS A CarerRelationship
    `the person was ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `child benefit was awarded to another person, B, in respect of the child (or each child) cared for, and for the week in which the care was provided` IS A BOOLEAN
    `B's earnings factors, other than those derived from a Class 3 contribution credit awarded under regulation 34` IS A NUMBER
    `the qualifying earnings factor for the year in which the week falls` IS A NUMBER
    `the person has made an application to the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (5) and regulation 39` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:430 | (3) The person (‘A’) referred to in paragraph (1) is not entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution unless—
-- src:431 | (a) child benefit was awarded to another person (‘B’) in respect of—
-- src:432 | (i) the child, or each child, for whom A provided care, and
-- src:433 | (ii) the week in which A provided that care,
-- src:434 | (b) B’s earnings factors, other than those derived from a Class 3 contribution credit awarded under regulation 34, exceed the qualifying earnings factor for the year in which the relevant week falls, and
-- src:435 | (c) A makes an application to the Secretary of State to be so credited in accordance with paragraph (5) and regulation 39.
@ref Regulation 35(3) (src:430-435)
GIVEN facts IS A ChildCareFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 35(3): the person is not barred from being credited` facts MEANS
        facts's `child benefit was awarded to another person, B, in respect of the child (or each child) cared for, and for the week in which the care was provided`
    AND facts's `B's earnings factors, other than those derived from a Class 3 contribution credit awarded under regulation 34` GREATER THAN facts's `the qualifying earnings factor for the year in which the week falls`
    AND facts's `the person has made an application to the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (5) and regulation 39`

-- src:426 | (2) The conditions are that in the relevant week the person—
-- src:427 | (a) provided care in respect of a child under the age of 12,
-- src:428 | (b) is, in relation to that child, a person specified in paragraph (6), and
-- src:429 | (c) was ordinarily resident in Great Britain.
@ref Regulation 35(2) (src:426-429)
GIVEN facts IS A ChildCareFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 35(2): the conditions are satisfied` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person provided care in the week in respect of a child under the age of 12`
    AND `regulation 35(6): the relationship is one the paragraph specifies` (facts's `the person's relationship to the child`)
    AND facts's `the person was ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week`

-- src:425 | (1) Subject to paragraphs (3) and (4), a person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of a week (“the relevant week”) in which the conditions in paragraph (2) are satisfied.
@ref Regulation 35(1) (src:425)
GIVEN facts IS A ChildCareFacts
      election IS A CarerElection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 35(1): the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` facts election MEANS
        `regulation 35(2): the conditions are satisfied` facts
    AND `regulation 35(3): the person is not barred from being credited` facts
    AND (CONSIDER election
         WHEN `no other person can satisfy paragraph (3)(a)(i), so paragraph (4) does not arise` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the person is the carer credited` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `another carer is the carer credited` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the Secretary of State has not yet decided which carer is credited` THEN FALSE)

§§§ `Regulation 36: credits for being a foster parent`

DECLARE FosterApproval IS ONE OF
    `a foster parent approved in accordance with Part 5 (approval of foster parents) of the Fostering Services (England) Regulations 2011`
    `a kinship carer approved in accordance with Part 5 (kinship care) of the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009`
    `a foster carer approved in accordance with Part 7 (fostering) of the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009`
    `a foster parent approved in accordance with Part 2 (approvals and placements) of the Foster Placement (Children) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1996`
    `not approved in any of those ways`

-- src:464 | (2) For the purposes of this regulation, a foster parent is a person approved as—
-- src:465 | (a) a foster parent in accordance with Part 5 (approval of foster parents) of the Fostering Services (England) Regulations 2011,
-- src:466 | (b) a kinship carer in accordance with Part 5 (kinship care) of the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009,
-- src:467 | (c) a foster carer in accordance with Part 7 (fostering) of those Regulations, or
-- src:468 | (d) a foster parent in accordance with Part 2 (approvals and placements) of the Foster Placement (Children) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1996.
@ref Regulation 36(2) (src:464-468)
GIVEN approval IS A FosterApproval
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 36(2): the person is a foster parent` approval MEANS
    CONSIDER approval
    WHEN `not approved in any of those ways` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE FosterFacts HAS
    `how the person is approved` IS A FosterApproval
    `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an application to be credited is received by the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs in accordance with regulation 39` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:461 | (1) Subject to paragraph (3), a person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of a week in which the person is a foster parent and is—
-- src:462 | (a) ordinarily resident in Great Britain, and
-- src:463 | (b) not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody.
-- src:469 | (3) A person is not entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution under paragraph (1) unless an application to be so credited is received by the Commissioners for Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs in accordance with regulation 39.
@ref Regulation 36(1) and (3) (src:461-463) (src:469)
GIVEN facts IS A FosterFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 36: the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` facts MEANS
        `regulation 36(2): the person is a foster parent` (facts's `how the person is approved`)
    AND facts's `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week`
    AND NOT (facts's `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody`)
    AND facts's `an application to be credited is received by the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs in accordance with regulation 39`

§§§ `Regulation 37: credits for persons engaged in caring`

DECLARE BenefitOfPersonCaredFor IS ONE OF
    `attendance allowance in accordance with section 64 of the 1992 Act`
    `pension age disability payment in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024`
    `the care component of disability living allowance in accordance with section 72 of the 1992 Act, at the middle or highest rate`
    `an increase in the rate of disablement pension in accordance with section 104 of the 1992 Act`
    `a benefit payable as if the injury or disease were one for which a disablement pension would be payable on an assessment of 100 per cent., by virtue of the Pneumoconiosis, Byssinosis and Miscellaneous Diseases Benefit Scheme 1983 or regulations made under section 64(3) of the 2012 Act`
    `a constant attendance allowance payable by virtue of article 8 of the Naval, Military and Air Forces etc. (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 2006 or article 14 of the Personal Injuries (Civilians) Scheme 1983`
    `the daily living component of personal independence payment in accordance with section 78 of the 2012 Act`
    `armed forces independence payment in accordance with the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011`
    `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11 of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021`
    `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate in accordance with regulation 5 of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022`
    `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025`
    `no benefit that regulation 37(4) lists`

-- src:480 | (4) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(a)(i), “relevant benefit” means—
-- src:481 | (a) attendance allowance in accordance with section 64 of the 1992 Act;
-- src:482 | (aa) pension age disability payment in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024;
-- src:483 | (b) the care component of disability living allowance in accordance with section 72 of the 1992 Act, at the middle or highest rate prescribed in accordance with subsection (3) of that section;
-- src:484 | (c) an increase in the rate of disablement pension in accordance with section 104 of the 1992 Act;
-- src:485 | (d) any benefit which is payable as if an injury or disease were one in respect of which a disablement pension would for the time being be payable in respect of an assessment of 100 per cent., by virtue of—
-- src:486 | (i) the Pneumoconiosis, Byssinosis and Miscellaneous Diseases Benefit Scheme 1983; or
-- src:487 | (ii) regulations made under section 64(3) of the 2012 Act (injuries arising before 5 July 1948);
-- src:488 | (e) a constant attendance allowance payable by virtue of—
-- src:489 | (i) article 8 (constant attendance allowance) of the Naval, Military and Air Forces etc. (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 2006; or
-- src:490 | (ii) article 14 (constant attendance allowance) of the Personal Injuries (Civilians) Scheme 1983;
-- src:491 | (f) the daily living component of personal independence payment in accordance with section 78 of the 2012 Act;
-- src:492 | (g) armed forces independence payment in accordance with the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011.
-- src:493 | (h) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11 of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021;
-- src:494 | (i) the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate payable in accordance with regulation 5 of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022;
-- src:495 | (j) the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025.
@ref Regulation 37(4) (src:480-495)
GIVEN benefit IS A BenefitOfPersonCaredFor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` benefit MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `no benefit that regulation 37(4) lists` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE CaringFacts HAS
    `the total number of hours the person cares for another person or persons in the week` IS A NUMBER
    `the benefit each person cared for is entitled to for the week` IS A LIST OF BenefitOfPersonCaredFor
    `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is not ordinarily resident in Great Britain for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an application to be credited is received by the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (6) and regulation 39` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:473 | (a) caring for another person or persons for a total of 20 or more hours in that week and—
-- src:474 | (i) that other person is, or each of the persons cared for are, entitled to a relevant benefit for that week, or
-- src:475 | (ii) the Secretary of State considers that level of care to be appropriate; or
@ref Regulation 37(2)(a) (src:473-475)
GIVEN facts IS A CaringFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 37(2)(a): the person cares for 20 or more hours at an appropriate level` facts MEANS
        facts's `the total number of hours the person cares for another person or persons in the week` AT LEAST 20
    AND (    (    count (facts's `the benefit each person cared for is entitled to for the week`) GREATER THAN 0
              AND all (GIVEN benefit YIELD `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` benefit) (facts's `the benefit each person cared for is entitled to for the week`))
         OR facts's `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate`)

-- src:476 | (b) a person to whom one or more of paragraphs 4 to 6 (persons caring for another person) of Schedule 1B (prescribed categories of person) to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies.
@ref Regulation 37(2)(b) (src:476)
GIVEN facts IS A CaringFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 37(2)(b): the person is within Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987` facts MEANS
    facts's `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to the person`

-- src:477 | (3) A person is not engaged in caring for the purposes of this regulation during any period in respect of which the person is—
-- src:478 | (a) not ordinarily resident in Great Britain, or
-- src:479 | (b) undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody.
@ref Regulation 37(3) (src:477-479)
GIVEN facts IS A CaringFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 37(3): the person is not engaged in caring during the period` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is not ordinarily resident in Great Britain for the period`
    OR facts's `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period`

-- src:472 | (2) A person is engaged in caring in a week if the person is—
@ref Regulation 37(2) (src:472)
GIVEN facts IS A CaringFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 37(2): the person is engaged in caring in the week` facts MEANS
        (   `regulation 37(2)(a): the person cares for 20 or more hours at an appropriate level` facts
         OR `regulation 37(2)(b): the person is within Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987` facts)
    AND NOT (`regulation 37(3): the person is not engaged in caring during the period` facts)

DECLARE CaringApplication HAS
    `the application includes a declaration by the applicant that the applicant cares for a person or persons for 20 or more hours in a week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application includes the name and, where known, the national insurance number of each person cared for` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person cared for is entitled to a relevant benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application says which relevant benefit each person cared for is entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State has asked for a declaration as to the level of care required` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application includes a declaration signed by an appropriate person as to the level of care required for each person cared for` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Gloss, paragraph (7): an appropriate person is involved in the health or social care of
-- the person cared for, and is considered by the Secretary of State appropriate to make
-- the declaration.
-- src:502 | (7) For the purposes of paragraph (6)(d), an appropriate person is a person who is—
-- src:503 | (a) involved in the health care or social care of the person cared for, and
-- src:504 | (b) considered by the Secretary of State as appropriate to make a declaration as to the level of care required.
@ref Regulation 37(7) (src:502-504)
GIVEN `the person is involved in the health care or social care of the person cared for` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State considers the person appropriate to make a declaration as to the level of care required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 37(7): the person is an appropriate person` `the person is involved in the health care or social care of the person cared for` `the Secretary of State considers the person appropriate to make a declaration as to the level of care required` MEANS
    `the person is involved in the health care or social care of the person cared for` AND `the Secretary of State considers the person appropriate to make a declaration as to the level of care required`

-- src:497 | (6) An application under paragraph (5) must include—
-- src:498 | (a) a declaration by the applicant that the applicant cares for a person or persons for 20 or more hours in a week,
-- src:499 | (b) the name and, where known, the national insurance number of each person cared for,
-- src:500 | (c) where applicable, which relevant benefit each person cared for is entitled to, and
-- src:501 | (d) where requested by the Secretary of State, a declaration signed by an appropriate person as to the level of care which is required for each person cared for.
@ref Regulation 37(6) (src:497-501)
GIVEN application IS A CaringApplication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 37(6): the application has the required content` application MEANS
        application's `the application includes a declaration by the applicant that the applicant cares for a person or persons for 20 or more hours in a week`
    AND application's `the application includes the name and, where known, the national insurance number of each person cared for`
    AND (IF application's `a person cared for is entitled to a relevant benefit`
         THEN application's `the application says which relevant benefit each person cared for is entitled to`
         ELSE TRUE)
    AND (IF application's `the Secretary of State has asked for a declaration as to the level of care required`
         THEN application's `the application includes a declaration signed by an appropriate person as to the level of care required for each person cared for`
         ELSE TRUE)

-- Gloss, paragraph (8): the application requirement of (5) is lifted for a woman with a
-- reduced rate election in force. Paragraph (5) binds only a credit under (2)(a): a person
-- within (2)(b) needs no application at all (fork F36).
-- src:505 | (8) This paragraph applies in the case of a woman in respect of a week in any part of which an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force.
@ref Regulation 37(8) (src:505)
GIVEN facts IS A CaringFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 37(8): paragraph (8) applies` facts MEANS
    facts's `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week`

-- src:496 | (5) Except in a case to which paragraph (8) applies, a person is not entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution under paragraph (2)(a) unless an application to be so credited is received by the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (6) and regulation 39.
@ref Regulation 37(5) (src:496)
GIVEN facts IS A CaringFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 37(5): an application is required` facts MEANS
        `regulation 37(2)(a): the person cares for 20 or more hours at an appropriate level` facts
    AND NOT (`regulation 37(8): paragraph (8) applies` facts)

-- src:471 | (1) Subject to paragraph (5), a person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of a week in which the person is engaged in caring.
@ref Regulation 37(1) (src:471)
GIVEN facts IS A CaringFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 37(1): the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` facts MEANS
        `regulation 37(2): the person is engaged in caring in the week` facts
    AND (IF `regulation 37(2)(b): the person is within Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987` facts
         THEN TRUE
         ELSE (IF `regulation 37(5): an application is required` facts
               THEN facts's `an application to be credited is received by the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (6) and regulation 39`
               ELSE TRUE))

§§§ `Regulation 38: credits for an additional period for carers`

DECLARE AdditionalPeriodKind IS ONE OF
    `before the person becomes entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support`
    `after the week in which the person ceases to be entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support`
    `after the week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied`

DECLARE CreditedPeriod HAS
    `first day of the period` IS A DATE
    `last day of the period` IS A DATE

-- Gloss, paragraph (1): twelve weeks (84 days, fork F33): ending the day before the date the
-- person becomes entitled, or starting the day after the end of the week in which the
-- entitlement or the caring ceases. The date taken is the date of becoming entitled for the
-- first kind and the last day of the week in which it ceases for the other two.
-- src:507 | (1) A person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution for a period of 12 weeks—
-- src:508 | (a) prior to the date on which that person becomes entitled to carer’s allowance by virtue of subsection (1) of section 70 of the 1992 Act or the carer support payment component of carer support given in accordance with the Carer’s Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023;
-- src:509 | (b) subject to paragraph (2), following the end of the week in which that person ceases to be entitled to carer’s allowance by virtue of that subsection or the carer support payment component of carer support by virtue of those Regulations;
-- src:510 | (c) following the end of a week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied.
@ref Regulation 38(1) (src:507-510)
GIVEN kind IS A AdditionalPeriodKind
      date IS A DATE
GIVETH A CreditedPeriod
`regulation 38(1): the period of 12 weeks` kind date MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `before the person becomes entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` THEN
        CreditedPeriod WITH
            `first day of the period` IS date MINUS 84
            `last day of the period` IS date MINUS 1
    OTHERWISE
        CreditedPeriod WITH
            `first day of the period` IS date PLUS 1
            `last day of the period` IS date PLUS 84

-- src:511 | (2) A person is not entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution under paragraph (1)(b) in a week in respect of which that person is entitled under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations to be credited with contributions by virtue of being entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the 1992 Act or the carer support payment component of carer support given in accordance with the Carer’s Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023.
@ref Regulation 38(2) (src:511)
GIVEN kind IS A AdditionalPeriodKind
      `the person is entitled for the week to be credited under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations by virtue of an allowance under section 70 of the 1992 Act or the carer support payment component of carer support` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 38(2): the week is excluded from the credit` kind `the person is entitled for the week to be credited under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations by virtue of an allowance under section 70 of the 1992 Act or the carer support payment component of carer support` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `after the week in which the person ceases to be entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` THEN
        `the person is entitled for the week to be credited under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations by virtue of an allowance under section 70 of the 1992 Act or the carer support payment component of carer support`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The day is within the period, and the person is not shut out by paragraph (2).
@ref Regulation 38(1) and (2) (src:507-511)
GIVEN kind IS A AdditionalPeriodKind
      date IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
      excluded IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 38: the day is credited` kind date day excluded MEANS
        day AT LEAST (`regulation 38(1): the period of 12 weeks` kind date)'s `first day of the period`
    AND day AT MOST (`regulation 38(1): the period of 12 weeks` kind date)'s `last day of the period`
    AND NOT excluded

§§§ `Regulation 39: time limit for applications`

DECLARE KindOfApplication IS ONE OF
    `an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37`
    `an application under regulation 35`

DECLARE ApplicationTimeFacts HAS
    `the kind of application` IS A KindOfApplication
    `the first day of a week which is the subject of the application` IS A DATE
    `the date the application is received` IS A DATE
    `the last day of any further time that the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs consider reasonable in the circumstances` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- Gloss: "the year following that in which the week falls" is the tax year after the one in
-- which the week begins (regulation 25(3)); an application received on the last day of that
-- year is received before the year has ended (fork F32).
-- src:514 | (a) where the application is under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37—
-- src:515 | (i) before the end of the year following that in which a week, which is the subject of the application, falls, or
-- src:516 | (ii) within such further time as the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs, as the case may be, consider reasonable in the circumstances, or
@ref Regulation 39(a) (src:514-516)
GIVEN facts IS A ApplicationTimeFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 39(a): the application is received in time` facts MEANS
        facts's `the date the application is received` AT MOST `the last day of the tax year` (taxYear PLUS 1)
    OR (CONSIDER facts's `the last day of any further time that the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs consider reasonable in the circumstances`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST furtherTime THEN facts's `the date the application is received` AT MOST furtherTime)
    WHERE
        taxYear MEANS `regulation 25(3): the tax year in which the week falls` (facts's `the first day of a week which is the subject of the application`)

-- Gloss: as written, an application under regulation 35 must be received AFTER the end of
-- the year in which the week falls, and the text gives no latest date (fork F31).
-- src:517 | (b) where the application is under regulation 35, after the end of the year in which a week, which is the subject of the application, falls.
@ref Regulation 39(b) (src:517)
GIVEN facts IS A ApplicationTimeFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 39(b): the application is received after the end of the year` facts MEANS
    facts's `the date the application is received` GREATER THAN `the last day of the tax year` (`regulation 25(3): the tax year in which the week falls` (facts's `the first day of a week which is the subject of the application`))

-- src:513 | An application must be received—
@ref Regulation 39 (src:513)
GIVEN facts IS A ApplicationTimeFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 39: the application is received in time` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the kind of application`
    WHEN `an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37` THEN `regulation 39(a): the application is received in time` facts
    WHEN `an application under regulation 35` THEN `regulation 39(b): the application is received after the end of the year` facts
